sweet-el2-report (SPEC-EL2-PROXY-PROBE 3.4 (b) design items 2-6, decision W24 option (b)): with boot-arg sweetel2=1 one kernel thread asks the shim's resident EL2 for its counters with `hvc #0x5345` (x0 = 0x53454C3200000001) at start and every 60 s and prints
`SWEET EL2: vm=V gaps=G traps=T bound=B up=<ms>` (x0 = 0x53454C32000000AA is the answer, x1 = HCR_EL2.VM, x2 = gaps, x3 = traps, x4 = bound). Why: under the shim's B2 build (`--el2-trap --boot-xnu`, stage 2 kept on across the jump) a stage-2 map
hole clears VM and retries natively, and the shim printer never runs again once XNU owns the CPU, so without this call a silent stage-2 drop would read as "XNU runs with stage 2 on" (rule 8). First line: `SWEET EL2: bootflags 0x<16 hex>`. Checks, each loud: boot_args.bootFlags bit 62 missing ->
`SWEET GAP: el2 report: sweetel2=1 but the shim reports no resident EL2` (no hvc: without a resident EL2 the hvc would reach the shim's EL1 vectors, SPEC 1.2); ml_get_cpu_count() != 1 (checked once, osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c:954-1016,:1184-1187) ->
`SWEET GAP: el2 report: N cpus, needs cpus=1` (patch 0063 rewrites the EL2 registers on secondaries); no answer -> `SWEET GAP: el2 report: no answer x0=<hex>` and the thread stops. Default (sweetel2 absent or 0): one PE_parse_boot_argn read, no thread, no
hvc executed. New bsd/dev/sweet_el2.c + bsd/conf/files entry; started from sweet_ufs_init next to sweet_cpustat_start (bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c, inside its ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET block). PE_state.bootArgs is a kernel VA (osfmk/arm/arm_init.c:357-358
BootArgs = &const_boot_args; pexpert/arm/pe_init.c:403) and carries bootFlags (pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h:77). Guarded by ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET. Not compiled locally, not run on hardware.

